#*: {{quote|ang|''Ġif þū tōdǣlst '''hwæt''' on fēower, sē fēorða dǣl biþ quadrans ġeċīeġed, and þā ōðre dōdrantēs bēoþ ġenemnede.''|If you divide '''something''' into fours, one part is called a ''quadrans'' (Latin for ‘one fourth’), and the other three are called ''dodrantes'' (Latin for ‘three fourths’).}}
