# [[who]] (in questions and implied questions about ''who'' someone is)
#* '''late 10th century''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], ''[[w:Old English Hexateuch|the Old English Hexateuch]]'', [https://books.google.com/books?id=QrZUAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA68 Genesis 27:32]
#*: {{quote|ang|''Þā cwæþ Isaāc, “'''Hwæt''' eart þū?” Hē andwyrde and cwæþ, “Iċ eom Ēsau.”''|Then Isaac said, “'''Who''' are you?” He answered and said, “I'm Esau.”}}
#* '''c. 990''', ''{{w|Wessex Gospels}}'', [https://archive.org/stream/dahalgangodspelo00thor#page/n243/mode/2up John 21:12]
#*: {{quote|ang|''Nān þāra þe þǣr sæt ne dorste hine āscian '''hwæt''' hē wǣre. Hīe wisson þæt hit wæs Dryhten.''|No one sitting there dared to ask him '''who''' he was. They knew it was the Lord.}}
#* '''c. 992''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://books.google.com/books?id=2xobVW92JLcC&pg=PA336 “The Second Sunday After Pentecost”]
#*: {{quote|ang|''Ġif iċ wisse '''hwæt''' hē wǣre, iċ wolde liċġan æt his fōtum.''|If I'd known '''who''' he was, I would have lain at his feet.}}
#* '''c. 992''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://books.google.com/books?id=m2hVAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA482 “The Passion of the Apostles Simon and Jude”]
#*: {{quote|ang|''Sē ealdormann hīe befræġn '''hwæt''' hīe wǣren, oþþe hwanon hīe cōmen, oþþe hwȳ hīe þæder cōmen.''|The general asked them '''who''' they were, where they came from, and why they came there. }}
#* '''c. 990''', ''{{w|Wessex Gospels}}'', [https://archive.org/stream/dahalgangodspelo00thor#page/n211/mode/2up John 8:52-53]
#*: {{quote|ang|''Þā cwǣdon þā Iūdēas, “Nū wē witon þæt þū eart wōd. Ābrahām wæs dēad, and þā wītegan, and þū cwist, ‘Ġif hwā mīn word ġehielt, ne biþ hē nǣfre dēad.’ Cwist þū þæt þū sīe mǣrra þonne ūre fæder Ābrahām, þe wæs dēad? And þā wītegan wǣron dēade! '''Hwæt''' þyncþ þē þæt þū sīe?”''|Then the Jews said, “Now we ''know'' you’re crazy. Abraham died, and so did the prophets, and you say, ‘If anyone keeps my word, they will never die.’ Are you saying you’re greater than our father Abraham, who died? And the prophets died! '''Who''' do you think you are?”}}

