=====Usage notes=====
Beginning with Thorkelin's translation of Beowulf and the work of Jacob Grimm, scholars have presumed 'hwæt' may have had the capacity to appear as an interjection. However, in recent decades, this assumption has been demonstrated to be false. Hwæt does not behave syntactically as an interjection, it is not listed by Aelfric as an OE interjection, and it appears zero times in 85 glosses of Latin [[ecce]]. See the Walkden article in References for more.

